It is because the following proposition is given as an axiom in the=20
universe of discourse (UD1) on the current topic.
P1:=20
ro'oi da poi ke'a me lo sidbo ku'o su'oi de zo'u de me da ijenai da me de

In this universe of discourse, the following proposition is a theorem.
P2:
naku ro'oi da poi ke'a me lo sidbo zo'u lo sidbo cu me da

As long as talking about UD1, we are forced to think that P2, that is,=20
there is no individual {lo sidbo}, because it is a proved theorem.

On the other hand, it is also possible that we talk about such a universe=
=20
of discourse (UD2) that the following proposition is an axiom or a theorem.
P3:
ro'oi da poi ke'a me lo sidbo zo'u lo sidbo cu me da

In UD2, {lo sidbo} is an individual, and a negation of P1 is proved.

Because neither P1 nor P3 is tautology, we are not forced to think that one=
=20
of them is always true for all the universes of discourse. We have freedom=
=20
to choose non-logical axioms and a universe of discourse according to=20
context.


